<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul fin ministry seeks input on financial reform.</title>
<headline>Seoul fin ministry seeks input on financial reform.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's finance ministry said on Thursday it would seek public input on draft financial reforms being promoted by the ministry and a presidential panel before submitting legislation to parliament.</p>
<p>&quot;We will hear opinions about the financial reform plan we are now promoting before revision of the relevant laws,&quot; said a ministry official.</p>
<p>The ministry said the draft would be considered by economic ministers, vice-ministers and cabinet members before legislation is submitted to parliament in mid-August.</p>
</text>
